## Module 6 – EV Charging Controller

### Objective
Introduce a simulated Electric Vehicle (EV) charging subsystem that integrates with the existing energy management system while respecting battery reserve requirements and available solar energy.

### Features
- Simulated EV connection status
- Simulated EV State of Charge (SOC)
- EV charging state (Charging / Waiting / Disconnected)
- Configurable EV charging power
- Battery reserve protection before EV charging
- OLED displays EV charging status and SOC

### Engineering Problem
When both the facility battery and an EV require charging, the controller must determine which receives available solar energy first while ensuring the facility maintains sufficient backup energy.

### Solution
A priority-based charging strategy was implemented. The controller first maintains the Battery Energy Storage System (BESS) reserve before permitting EV charging. Once the reserve threshold is satisfied and sufficient excess solar power is available, the EV charging process begins.

